-- title:
--   From an explicit q-adic family to the formal-group package
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq 2$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $E_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, and let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $\mathcal E$ be a Weierstrass curve over $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$ whose discriminant $\Delta$ is a unit and which reduces to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$. Assume that the Hasse invariant in weight $q$ of the reduction $\mathcal E \otimes k\llbracket X\rrbracket$ along `PowerSeries.map res₀` — defined as the coefficient of degree $q-1$ in the $((q-1)/2)$-th power of the two-torsion polynomial — has vanishing constant coefficient and non-zero coefficient of $X$. Assume furthermore that there are $a_0 \in W_0$, an integer $e \geq 1$ and a unit $u_2$ of $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$ with $j(\mathcal E) - a_0 = u_2 X^{e}$, where $j(\mathcal E)$ is `jOfUnit` for the given unit $\Delta$. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E'$ over $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$ with unit discriminant reducing to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, and a formal group $F_u$ over $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$ which is commutative, whose defining two-variable power series is $\mathcal E'$'s `formalGroupLawFixed`, and which is a base change of the data of `E₀.formalGroup` in the sense that the latter's power series equals the image of $F_u$'s under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, such that, writing $\gamma \in W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$ for the coefficient of $X^{q}$ in the $q$-th iterate `nthSeries q` of $F_u$ (the series defined by $[0] = 0$, $[n+1] = F_u([n], X)$), one has: the coefficient of $X$ in $\gamma$ is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$; $\gamma - u_1 X$ lies in the ideal generated by $q$ for some unit $u_1$ of $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$; and $j(\mathcal E') - a_0' = u_2' X^{e'}$ for some $a_0' \in W_0$, some $e' \geq 1$ and some unit $u_2'$ of $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$.
--
--   This is the step that converts an explicitly given one-parameter Weierstrass family over $W_0\llbracket X\rrbracket$, for which only the vanishing to exact order one of the mod-$q$ Hasse invariant and the monomial shape of $j$ have to be checked, into the formal-group package (commutative Weierstrass formal group lifting $\hat E_0$, multiplication-by-$q$ series with $X^q$-coefficient a unit multiple of $X$ modulo $q$, and monomial $j$) required downstream; the conclusion has exactly the shape of the existential package consumed there. It is used by the variant [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_X_pow_of_coeff_hasseInvariant_map_variableChange`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_X_pow_of_coeff_hasseInvariant_map_variableChange), which obtains the curve $\mathcal E'$ from $\mathcal E$ by a rescaling of the parameter.
